    {
      "key": "ScreenRecorder",
      "kind": "class",
      "doc": {
        "summary": "Records one source as silent SDR H.264/MP4 using a native capture backend.",
        "details": "Calls use the host UI thread. Start/Stop/Cancel report acceptance, not completion. Keep the recorder alive until a terminal event. Destruction discards unfinished output and suppresses further events; it never implicitly saves. No listener is required for recording to progress. Output dimensions are fixed by the first frame; resized content is fitted with black bars. Requested crops must remain in bounds.\n\n```cpp\nauto recorder = std::make_shared<ScreenRecorder>();\nauto source = CaptureSource::FromDisplay(DisplayManager::GetInstance().GetPrimary());\nbool accepted = recorder->Start(source, \"/tmp/recording.mp4\", {});\n// Retain recorder; after StartedEvent call Stop and await a terminal event.\n```",
        "notes": [
          {
            "kind": "note",
            "text": "Platform availability:\n- macOS: ⚠️ macOS 14+ ScreenCaptureKit and AVAssetWriter; permission required\n- Windows: ⚠️ Windows 10 2004+ Graphics Capture and Media Foundation H.264 encoder\n- Linux: ❌ Not implemented - Start returns false\n- Android: ❌ Not implemented - Start returns false\n- iOS: ❌ Not implemented - Start returns false\n- OpenHarmony: ❌ Not implemented - Start returns false"
          }
        ]
      },
